                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=0
                                                               ; ONE BLOCK FOLDED INTO A GHASH  which is Y = (Y xor X)
                                                               ; dot H;
;
                                                               ; NIST SP 800_38D section 6 point 4; aes/gcm128 does
                                                               ; this three times: over the associated data  over the
                                                               ; ciphertext  and over the length block; The three are
                                                               ; the same seven hundred lines  so they are one file;
;
                                                               ; Entered and left at the caller's own nought; the
                                                               ; block to fold is at
; @0x3db:0x3ea and is SPENT  the accumulator at @0x3eb:0x3fa is replaced  and
                                                               ; the subkey at @0x3a5:0x3b4 is COPIED and survives;
;
                                                               ; THE SUBKEY SURVIVES AND THE BLOCK DOES NOT  and that
                                                               ; asymmetry is the whole of the bookkeeping here;
                                                               ; block/ghashmul spends both of ITS operands  so the
                                                               ; accumulator MOVES into the bit source and the subkey
                                                               ; is COPIED into the value; A GCM folds as many blocks
                                                               ; as the message has and every one of them wants H
                                                               ; again;
;
                                                               ; THE BLOCK IS LEFT CLEAR  which is what lets the
                                                               ; caller build the next one by sliding bytes into it
                                                               ; without clearing first; the exclusive or consumes it
                                                               ; a byte at a time on a conveyor;
;
                                                               ; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE; this block is included at
                                                               ; offset nought three times so they resolve to the
                                                               ; addresses aes/gcm128's tape map names;
;
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=0

; ============================================================ ; the accumulator takes the block  sixteen turns on two
                                                               ; conveyors
